          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Pick the Battery Platform First
          </h2>

          <p>
            An impact driver is usually the second cordless tool anyone buys, after a drill, and that makes it a platform decision rather than a tool decision. Batteries do not cross brands. A Milwaukee M18 pack will not fit a DeWalt 20V MAX tool, and third-party adapters that claim otherwise can void warranties and bypass the protection electronics that stop a pack from overheating. Whatever you buy here, you are also choosing what your saw, your sander and your next drill will run on.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you already own a drill on one of these platforms, buy the bare impact driver for it and stop reading spec sheets. The gap between the best and the fourth-best 18V driver on this list is far smaller than the cost of a second set of batteries and a second charger. If you are starting from nothing, our <a href="/best-cordless-tool-brand/">cordless tool brand rankings</a> go through each platform in turn, and the <a href="/milwaukee-vs-dewalt/">Milwaukee vs DeWalt</a> comparison covers the two systems most professionals end up choosing between.
          </p>

          <p>
            The platform also decides what you can add later. A homeowner who will eventually want a string trimmer, a leaf blower and a shop vacuum is better served by a platform with a broad, affordable catalog than by the one with the fastest driver. Ryobi ONE+ wins that argument on breadth and price. Milwaukee and DeWalt win it on heavy-duty tools and the depth of their professional ranges. Makita sits between them, with especially good compact tools and a very large 18V LXT line.
          </p>

          <p>
            There is one more reason to think about the platform first, and it is the circular saw. If a deck, a fence or a shed is the reason you are buying an impact driver, a cordless saw is probably next on the list, and it draws far more current than any driver. Read our <a href="/best-cordless-circular-saw/">best cordless circular saw</a> guide before you commit, because the saw is where battery capacity and platform strength actually start to matter.
          </p>

